## Reviewer got it wrong — not applied as suggested
- mn-a 3. The visible standard name was already «Төрөл бүрийн орлогын эх үүсвэрийн суутгалын хувийн хэм хэмжээ». The URL is flno=3, and the English link text itself says “Article 10”. Dropping the 10 fails the number check. The label keeps «10 дугаар зүйл».
- mn-a 26 and the money pattern in the verdict. «1,57 сая» uses a decimal comma. For mn the checker parses a comma as thousands and a point as the decimal (`0.5`). «TWD 1.57M» is pinned. Column amounts stay `TWD 500,000`.
- mn-a 24 and mn-b 14. Q16–Q20 are body lines, and the U+200B lines are non-empty blocks that match the Korean source. Removing them, or promoting them to headings, changes the block or ZWSP count. 013 failed the checker at ZWSP 5 → 4 until the removed character was put back.
- mn-b 9. «хоёр дахь» is the right meaning, and it is also a counted 2. Korean «두 번째» is not in the number lexicon, so the file would gain an extra 2. «менежерээс өөр гадаадын иргэн» keeps the meaning without a new number.
- mn-b 18. Removing «1 дахин» drops the digit in Korean «최대 1배». «нэг дахин» would still read as “once”. The sentence now says the cap does not exceed actual harm and still has «1 дахин».
- mn-b 23. The suggested sentence joins three paragraphs. English splits the same thought across three paragraphs. Each Mongolian paragraph is now a sentence; they were not merged.
